The Elder Scrolls II: Daggerfall, The Elder Scrolls: Arena and The Elder
Scrolls III: Morrowind are the property of Bethesda Softworks. The MIT License
does not cover any of their content.

The game reads Daggerfall's files from the player's own copy at runtime, and
those files never enter this repository. One exception: vendor/dfu-quests
carries Daggerfall Unity's text form of the original game's quests, as
Daggerfall Unity distributes it. The quests themselves are Bethesda's work.

For the optional 3D layer, the game reads Morrowind's files from the player's
own copy at runtime. Those files never enter this repository.

Earlier versions read the places past the Iliac Bay from the player's copy of
Arena. Nothing of Arena is read now.
